          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What would the alternative be first?",
          "answer": "The guidance I found does not say what the first-line alternative to medicine is for cholesterol. The lipid guidance, \"Lipids: screening intervals, risk stratification and statin initiation,\" covers how screening is done and how 10-year risk drives the treatment decision. It does not describe lifestyle measures or other options to try before medicine.\n\nThe other documents my search returned don't answer this either. The hypertension guidance mentions lifestyle measures first, but it is about blood pressure, not cholesterol. The anxiety and diabetes documents cover other conditions.\n\nYour clinician can tell you whether lifestyle changes are a reasonable first step for you, and what the options and trade-offs are. Ask them which options fit your estimated 10-year risk and your other health factors.\n\nIf you develop chest pain, pain spreading to the arm, jaw or back, sudden shortness of breath, fainting, or sudden weakness or trouble speaking, call your local emergency number right away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
